# Logistics & Order Performance Analysis — DataCo Dataset

**How much profit is at risk from late deliveries, and where should we focus to protect it?**

This project analyses 180,000+ orders from the DataCo Smart Supply 
Chain dataset to connect delivery performance directly to profit — 
turning four separate analyses into one executive story.

**Tools:** SQL (SQLite / DBeaver), Google Looker Studio, Excel  
**Dataset:** [DataCo Smart Supply Chain — Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/shashwatwork/dataco-smart-supply-chain-for-big-data-analysis)

## The Headline
**54% of all profit — around $2.1M — flows through orders that 
arrive late.** This has held steady for three years, pointing to a 
systemic issue rather than a one-off.

## The Story (KPI → Action)
This dashboard follows a decision-making funnel:

- **KPIs** — 54% of profit is exposed to late delivery
- **Trend** — the problem has stayed flat for 3 years, not improving
- **Drivers** — the 5 highest-profit categories carry the most exposure
- **Exception** — First Class shipping fails 95% of the time
- **Action** — where to focus first to protect profit

## Key Recommendation
Start with First and Second Class shipping — 35% of orders but 55% 
of profit at risk. Tune Standard Class in parallel. Because risk is 
uniform across categories, departments, and regions, investigate 
shared fulfilment and platform processes rather than individual teams.

